Where [See it live](showcase.tmd) shows one capability at a time, the gallery shows
**entire projects**, each a real `.tmd` source tree rendered by Taliesin.

## Probabilistic Modeling: a short course

A lecturer's interactive lecture notes. A numbered **book** whose figures and display
equations number and cross-reference **across chapters**, real **math** rendered offline,
and an executable Python cell: the whole authoring surface a course needs, in one
project.

[Open the course &rarr;](gallery/course/)

## Tarn: a library documentation site

The docs for a small dataframe library. A numbered **book** split into a Guide and an
API **Reference**, with per-package-manager and per-OS install instructions, a
line-by-line reading of the core query, version and deprecation **callouts**, and
full-text **Cmd-K search** that spans every page: the whole shape of a real open-source
documentation site.

[Open the docs &rarr;](gallery/tarn/)

## Gradient descent, by hand

An interactive explainer, the kind you poke at. One long page where a **reactive
graphic** redraws as you drag the starting point and work three sliders, a five-scene
walk-through of the descent whose figure you step through yourself, a live **Observable
Plot** chart wired to the same controls, and the derivation in real **math** alongside:
an explorable explanation with every moving part authored in `.tmd`.

[Open the explainer &rarr;](gallery/descent/)

## Queue latency, Q3: a computational report

A quarterly analytics readout, and the only exhibit here whose pages **run code** as
they build. The data is cleaned, charted and modelled in **Python**, executing against
one committed dataset. The figures and coefficient tables are generated by the report,
numbered in document order, and cross-referenced from the prose and from a second page.

[Open the readout &rarr;](gallery/analyst/)

